{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Your heart.</b> It speaks of terror in his soul." "<b>Where is the scribe.</b> He is the one who writes, like [how much is] every man's punishment." "<b>Where is the one who weighs, where is the scribe of towers.</b> From the root of counting, for they imposed a punishment upon every tower."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra likens סופר to one who reckons; the bracketed כמה ('how much') is supplied per the editor's correction (צ\"ל) of the printed כמו."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:31.856980068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}